Here’s how you can invoke the helper to build the `CodeTree` for a non‑static converter method called `convertValue`.  
The helper expects the method as an `ExecutableElement` (you can just pass its name as a string), the name of the frame variable, and the name of the variable that will receive the conversion result.

```java
// Build the CodeTree that calls the non‑static method `convertValue`
//   - frame parameter:  frameVar
//   - return value:     returnValueCode
CodeTree callTree = functions.InstrumentableProcessor_createCallConverter({
    converterMethod: "convertValue",   // ExecutableElement (string form)
    frameParameterName: "frameVar",    // name of the frame variable
    returnName: "returnValueCode"      // name of the return value variable
});
```

`callTree` now contains the AST fragment that will invoke `convertValue(frameVar)` and assign its result to `returnValueCode`. You can insert this tree into your Truffle DSL processor wherever the conversion call is needed.

